    "25786": {
        "order_id": 7,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "Variation Types",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2014",
        "question_text": "<p>If $y$ varies directly as $x$ and $y = 10$ when $x = 2$, find the value of $y$ when $x = 5$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Since $y$ varies directly as $x$, $y = kx$ for some constant $k$.<br>Given $y = 10$ when $x = 2$, substitute to find $k$: $10 = k(2) \\implies k = 5$.<br>Thus, $y = 5x$. When $x = 5$, $y = 5(5) = 25$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
