        "topic": "Coordinate Geometry",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2014",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the equation of the line passing through the points $(1, 2)$ and $(3, 4)$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>First, find the slope $m$ of the line:<br>$m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} = \\frac{4 - 2}{3 - 1} = 1$.<br>Using the point-slope form: $y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$. Substitute $(1, 2)$:<br>$y - 2 = 1(x - 1) \\implies y = x + 1$.<br>The equation of the line is $y = x + 1$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
