        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2014",
        "question_text": "<p>If $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, find $\\cos \\theta$ for $0^\\circ < \\theta < 90^\\circ$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using the Pythagorean identity: $\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$.<br>Substitute $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$:<br>$\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1 \\implies \\frac{9}{25} + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$.<br>$\\cos^2 \\theta = 1 - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{16}{25} \\implies \\cos \\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$.</p>",
